course: dictionary
lesson: 14330
title: Things that block the way
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An obstruction is something that blocks a road, path, pipe or passage so that things cannot get through. Read the words around it to find the clue. «The fire exit was blocked by a pile of boxes, an obstruction that stopped everyone getting out.» The boxes are in the way, so an obstruction is something in the way.
explain: The word also means the act of stopping or delaying something on purpose. «The council was accused of obstruction when it delayed the new road for months.» Here obstruction is a deliberate action, not a thing you can touch.
explain: In sport, obstruction is a foul. «The referee gave a free kick for obstruction when a defender used his body to block the attacker.» In law, obstruction of justice means trying to stop the police or a court from doing their job. Always check the context to see which meaning fits.
fact: An obstruction is something that blocks a road, path, pipe or passage.
fact: «The nurse had to clear the obstruction from his throat.» A blocked throat is an obstruction in the body.
fact: Keep fire exits and stairs clear, because an obstruction can stop people getting out in an emergency.
fact: In football and hockey, obstruction means illegally blocking an opponent with your body.
fact: Obstruction of justice means trying to stop the police or a court from doing their job.
exercise: «The fire exit was blocked by a pile of boxes, an obstruction that stopped everyone getting out.» What is an obstruction here? | A happy shout | A fire drill | *Something that blocks the way | A kind of door
exercise: In football and hockey, what is obstruction? | Scoring a goal with your head | Kicking the ball out of play | Running very fast | *Illegally blocking an opponent with your body
exercise: «The nurse had to clear the obstruction from his throat.» What does clear mean here? | Say something loudly | Clean the window | Make a clear, quiet sound | *Remove the thing that is blocking
test: A tree fell across the road and stopped all the traffic. What was the tree? | A decoration | A bridge | *An obstruction | A tunnel
test: Obstruction of justice means what? | Being a judge in a court | Giving evidence in a trial | *Trying to stop the police or a court from doing their job | Helping the police catch a thief
exam: «The council was accused of obstruction when it delayed the new road on purpose.» What does obstruction mean here? | *Deliberately stopping or delaying something | Building a bridge | Running a race | Helping the road get built faster
